const moatWhy:Record<string,string[]>= {
  VRT:["Failure is extremely costly, so customers favour suppliers with proven engineering and uptime.","Servicing installed systems creates recurring revenue and keeps Vertiv close to future expansion plans.","An integrated offering reduces design complexity and the number of vendors customers must coordinate.","Higher rack densities increase cooling difficulty, making specialist knowledge more valuable.","Once equipment is tested and approved, changing suppliers introduces reliability and redesign risk.","New factories, trained technicians and worldwide support coverage cannot be replicated quickly."],
  GEV:["A large operating fleet produces decades of service work and proprietary performance knowledge.","Utilities prioritise reliability and regulatory acceptance, favouring suppliers with a long operating record.","Limited production capacity lets established manufacturers secure long backlogs and favourable contract terms.","Long asset lives turn each new installation into a durable customer and service relationship.","Fleet data improves maintenance, reliability and future designs in a way newcomers cannot easily match.","The cost, certification and time required to build utility-grade equipment restrict competition."],
  ETN:["Being designed into a facility early makes replacement costly once construction and approvals begin.","Customers can standardise on one trusted supplier across many critical electrical functions.","Distributor access and local engineering support make Eaton easier to specify, obtain and maintain.","Substituting approved components may require new testing, documentation and engineering work.","A growing installed base supports recurring replacement, upgrade and service demand.","Scale funds additional capacity and keeps a wider product range available than smaller rivals."],
  ASML:["Without ASML's EUV systems, chipmakers cannot economically manufacture the most advanced designs.","The machine combines thousands of interdependent breakthroughs that no single competitor can easily reproduce.","Joint roadmap planning makes ASML essential to customers years before a new process enters production.","Its specialist suppliers contribute unique components built through decades of close collaboration.","Fab processes are tuned around ASML tools, so replacing them would disrupt yields and production.","High-NA improves future chip scaling while increasing the technical and financial barrier to entry."],
  TSM:["High yields lower customers' cost per working chip and reduce the risk of product launches.","Customers can share sensitive designs without empowering a competing chip-product business.","Its volume allows enormous R&D and factory costs to be spread across many customers.","Every production run adds learning that improves yields and makes the next process ramp more dependable.","Packaging capacity is increasingly essential for combining processors and memory into complete AI systems.","Moving a chip design requires costly revalidation, new tooling and months of engineering work."],
  CDNS:["Only a few vendors can provide the complete, trusted toolchain needed for advanced chip design.","Engineers build processes and expertise around these tools, making mid-project changes unusually risky.","Selling design IP and system analysis deepens customer dependence beyond the core software suite.","A failed verification can delay a chip by months, so proven workflows outweigh small price differences.","More design activity produces data that can improve automation and engineering productivity.","As chips become more complex, customers need broader simulation and verification rather than fewer tools."],
  NVDA:["Developers can reuse familiar tools and libraries instead of rewriting workloads for another platform.","Customers receive a tested system, reducing the time and technical risk of assembling components themselves.","A larger user base attracts more developers, software support and optimisation for each new generation.","Years of libraries, documentation and trained developers make CUDA more than a hardware feature.","Fast product cycles force competitors to match improvements across chips, networking and software simultaneously.","Compatibility with existing code and infrastructure makes staying on the platform economically attractive."],
  AVGO:["Designing a custom accelerator requires years of collaboration, making established partnerships difficult to displace.","Proven networking technology is critical because slow data movement can waste expensive compute capacity.","Shared engineering and customer relationships allow Broadcom to sell more content into each platform.","Successful first-generation programs create trust and technical knowledge for later, larger deployments.","Advanced connectivity depends on specialised intellectual property developed over many product cycles.","Each completed program improves Broadcom's credibility when customers select partners for the next generation."],
  ANET:["A consistent operating system simplifies automation and management across thousands of network devices.","Customers trust Arista in environments where outages can idle very expensive cloud and AI infrastructure.","Close collaboration with hyperscalers helps products evolve around real operating requirements.","Monitoring, automation and staff knowledge built around EOS make a platform change operationally disruptive.","Maintaining one software foundation lets features and reliability improvements reach the whole portfolio.","Success in AI back-end networks expands Arista's role without abandoning its established Ethernet strength."],
  MSFT:["Microsoft can place AI directly inside tools that enterprises and developers already use daily.","Shared identity, permissions and data make its AI services easier to deploy securely across organisations.","Existing procurement relationships reduce the time and effort needed to adopt another Microsoft product.","Migrating core productivity and cloud systems would require substantial retraining, integration and operational change.","Workplace data gives agents the context needed to perform useful tasks rather than only answer questions.","Demand for applications drives Azure usage, while Azure capabilities make the applications more valuable."],
  AMZN:["Customers can build almost any workload without coordinating infrastructure across multiple providers.","Applications built around AWS services and APIs become expensive and technically difficult to migrate.","Purpose-built chips can improve cost, availability and performance for common AI workloads.","A very large customer base justifies continuous investment in regions, capacity and new services.","Partners and third-party software reduce implementation effort and make AWS more useful to customers.","Global operating experience enables AWS to provide capacity and reliability that smaller providers struggle to match."],
  GOOGL:["Google can introduce AI to billions of users without paying another platform for distribution.","Owning chips, infrastructure and models allows optimisation across the entire cost and performance stack.","User interactions provide feedback that improves product relevance and advertising effectiveness.","Embedding Gemini into established products makes adoption easier than asking users to learn a separate service.","Longstanding research teams and TPUs reduce dependence on external models and general-purpose hardware.","Advertising cash flow can fund the sustained model and infrastructure investment required to remain competitive."],
  META:["Meta can distribute assistants and AI features instantly across its global family of apps.","More engagement produces feedback that improves recommendations, which can create still more engagement.","Open access encourages developers to optimise and build around Llama rather than a competing model family.","Users, creators and relationships form networks that remain valuable even when individual features are copied.","AI improvements can translate quickly into better ad targeting, creative tools and advertiser returns.","Large infrastructure spending supports model development at a scale available to very few companies."],
  PLTR:["The ontology translates fragmented company data into objects and relationships that models can use safely.","Once software guides operational decisions, removal becomes more disruptive than replacing a reporting tool.","Security credentials and mission experience are important barriers in sensitive government environments.","Customer-specific models capture processes and institutional knowledge that accumulate throughout a deployment.","Replacing the platform can interrupt critical operations and require complex security reapproval.","Experience across deployments allows Palantir to solve similar problems faster for the next customer."],
  NOW:["Owning the workflow lets ServiceNow determine how requests, approvals and actions move through a company.","A common platform connects otherwise separate departments and reduces integration complexity.","Existing customers can adopt agents inside familiar processes without introducing a new operating layer.","Years of configuration and integrations make moving workflows to another platform expensive and risky.","Each added module contributes more context and makes the overall platform harder to replace.","Central governance makes automated actions safer, which is essential for enterprise adoption of agents."],
  CRM:["Salesforce sits close to revenue-generating work and stores information employees need every day.","Its salesforce can introduce new AI and data products through relationships with existing enterprise buyers.","Partners, applications and integrations make the platform useful beyond Salesforce's own products.","Historical customer data and customised processes are costly to move without disrupting commercial teams.","Unifying fragmented information gives agents better context across the entire customer relationship.","Agents become more valuable and defensible when they can act directly inside core sales and service processes."]
};
for(const [ticker,why] of Object.entries(moatWhy)) companies[ticker].moatWhy=why;
const moatContext:Record<string,string[]>= {
  VRT:["These operators cannot tolerate downtime, so proven reliability and service coverage heavily influence purchasing.","Competition is credible, but Vertiv differentiates through data-center specialisation and an integrated global offering.","Rising adoption would confirm that Vertiv remains central as rack densities increase.","Healthy conversion shows demand is real and that pricing power survives rapid capacity expansion.","Faster service growth would make revenue more recurring and deepen relationships with installed customers."],
  GEV:["Utilities and developers make multi-decade asset decisions, placing a premium on bankability and lifecycle support.","Peers have comparable engineering depth, making execution, available production slots and fleet economics decisive.","More orders would show that power scarcity is translating into durable equipment demand.","Backlog growth only strengthens the moat if GE Vernova can deliver reliably and profitably.","Higher service margins would prove the installed fleet is producing valuable recurring economics."],
  ETN:["Electrical systems are selected early in a project and must meet strict safety and reliability requirements.","Large rivals offer similar breadth, so product availability, channel access and specification wins determine share.","Order growth ahead of capacity would indicate customers continue to specify Eaton in new facilities.","Longer lead times and stable pricing suggest supply remains scarce and customer demand is resilient.","Share gains would show Eaton is expanding its role in the most technically demanding parts of power distribution."],
  ASML:["Only a handful of advanced chipmakers buy EUV, but each depends on ASML for its technology roadmap.","Older lithography alternatives cannot replace EUV at leading nodes, leaving ASML without a direct commercial peer.","Production adoption would validate both customer dependence and the next phase of ASML's roadmap.","Higher field productivity increases customer output and makes every installed system more economically valuable.","Sustained investment protects the knowledge gap that makes the monopoly difficult to challenge."],
  TSM:["Leading chip designers choose TSMC because yield, scale and dependable execution directly affect their own launches.","Samsung and Intel can compete technologically, but must match TSMC's yields, capacity and trusted foundry model.","A smooth ramp would confirm that process leadership is continuing at the next major node.","Capacity expansion shows whether TSMC can capture demand beyond wafer fabrication itself.","Repeated customer commitments indicate that rivals are not closing the gap enough to trigger switching."],
  CDNS:["Chip designers rely on these tools throughout development, making accuracy and workflow continuity mission-critical.","Synopsys is the closest peer; competition is largely between two entrenched ecosystems rather than new entrants.","Strong renewals show customers still view Cadence as embedded infrastructure rather than discretionary software.","Growth would demonstrate that Cadence is capturing more value from each increasingly complex design.","Production use matters more than pilots because it proves AI features improve real engineering economics."],
  NVDA:["Customers range from hyperscalers to governments, spreading demand across buyers that need rapid deployment at scale.","Alternatives can compete on chips, but must also overcome NVIDIA's software, networking and developer ecosystem.","Continued workload growth would show developers are not meaningfully migrating away from CUDA.","Broader system sales indicate NVIDIA is capturing more of the cluster rather than only the accelerator.","Smooth transitions demonstrate that customers remain willing to adopt NVIDIA's rapid product cadence."],
  AVGO:["A small group of hyperscalers buys at enormous scale and values partners capable of multi-year custom design programs.","Rivals can contest individual programs, but replacing Broadcom requires comparable IP and co-design execution.","More programs would reduce dependence on any single customer and validate Broadcom's repeatability.","Rising content means Broadcom benefits as clusters require more connectivity per accelerator.","Repeat wins are the clearest evidence that customer knowledge and trust create durable switching costs."],
  ANET:["Large cloud operators demand exceptional reliability and automation because network failures idle costly infrastructure.","Cisco and NVIDIA have scale, but Arista's consistent software architecture remains its main point of differentiation.","Back-end wins would show EOS and Ethernet can extend successfully into the fastest-growing network segment.","Diversification would make the moat less dependent on a few hyperscaler relationships.","Retention through upgrades confirms that operational switching costs persist across hardware generations."],
  MSFT:["Enterprises and developers already operate inside Microsoft's identity, productivity and cloud environments.","Rivals may lead in individual categories, but few can match Microsoft's combined infrastructure and application distribution.","Paid expansion would demonstrate that distribution is converting into incremental revenue, not only bundled usage.","Growth alongside new supply shows Microsoft can turn heavy investment into utilised, differentiated capacity.","Cross-product use would prove the ecosystem is reinforcing itself and raising customer switching costs."],
  AMZN:["AWS serves organisations of every size, giving it diversified demand and a large base for new services.","Azure and Google Cloud are formidable, so breadth, execution and customer economics must keep differentiating AWS.","Sustained workload growth shows customers still prefer the platform despite credible alternatives.","Production adoption would validate custom silicon as a cost and supply advantage rather than a niche option.","Usage beyond compute suggests AWS is deepening its role and increasing customer dependence on the ecosystem."],
  GOOGL:["Its buyer base spans advertisers, consumers and enterprises, allowing AI investment to support several revenue engines.","Competition is broad, but Google's combination of data, distribution, models and infrastructure is unusually complete.","Rising engagement would show that built-in distribution is translating into habitual usage.","Customer and profit growth would prove Google can monetise its technical advantage in enterprise markets.","Stable usage and monetisation would show generative answers are strengthening rather than cannibalising Search."],
  META:["Users create attention and data, while advertisers fund the platform—two groups that reinforce each other.","Rivals compete for time and advertising budgets, but recreating Meta's social graphs and reach is difficult.","Engagement gains show AI is improving the core network rather than functioning as an isolated feature.","Better advertiser returns convert technical progress directly into pricing power and budget share.","External adoption would show Llama is becoming an ecosystem with influence beyond Meta's own products."],
  PLTR:["Customers operate in complex, regulated environments where governance and dependable deployment matter more than generic tools.","Internal builds and cloud platforms are alternatives, but often require more integration and implementation responsibility.","Expansion into production indicates the ontology is becoming embedded in real operating decisions.","Strong retention demonstrates that accumulated workflows and data relationships create genuine switching costs.","Faster repeatable delivery would show Palantir can scale its advantage without relying on bespoke consulting."],
  NOW:["Large organisations use ServiceNow across departments, giving new agents access to established workflows and permissions.","Competitors own adjacent systems, but replacing ServiceNow means rebuilding deeply configured cross-company processes.","Higher renewal value would prove AI increases platform economics rather than merely protecting existing contracts.","Consolidation shows customers prefer one governed workflow layer over a collection of disconnected tools.","Completed production actions demonstrate that agents are trusted to do work, not simply generate suggestions."],
  CRM:["Commercial teams work inside Salesforce daily, giving new AI products immediate access to users and customer context.","Competitors attack different parts of the stack, but Salesforce retains an unusually broad CRM data footprint.","Paid usage would show customers see enough measurable value to move beyond experimentation.","Broader adoption makes customer data more unified and strengthens the foundation for useful agents.","Stable retention would indicate AI is reinforcing the platform despite pressure on traditional seat-based software."]
};
for(const [ticker,context] of Object.entries(moatContext)) companies[ticker].moatContext=context;
